    "title": "Ken Griffin's Plan to Move Historic Coconut Grove Home to Vizcaya Clears Key Vote - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Elena Vega ,\n6 hours ago Billionaire Ken Griffin's plan to uproot a 113-year-old Coconut Grove mansion and plant it on the grounds of Vizcaya just cleared a major hurdle. The Miami-Dade County Commission voted to let Mayor Daniella Levine Cava or her designee begin negotiating with Griffin over relocating Villa Serena, the Mediterranean-style home built for William Jennings Bryan, to Vizcaya Village. Read full article",
